    @* Phase 2.5 — Selection family (LipiCheckbox/-Group, LipiRadio/-Group, LipiToggle)
       and form utility patterns (lipi-form-row helpers). These ship via the deploy
       script but were never wired in App.razor — caused the LabelPosition.Left grid
       layout on LipiCheckboxGroup to silently fall back to default fieldset layout.
       Stage 1C of Phase 2.6.3 stabilisation closes this Phase 2.5 audit debt. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/lipi-selection-family.css?v=20260526" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/lipi-form-utilities.css?v=20260526" />

    @* Phase 2.6.1 — Layout components (LipiTabs + LipiAlert + LipiCard).
       Without these the tab/alert/card components render unstyled markup. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/lipi-tabs.css?v=20260526" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/lipi-alerts.css?v=20260526" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/lipi-cards.css?v=20260526" />

    @* Phase 2.6.2 — Overlay surfaces (LipiModal + LipiDrawer + LipiDynamicTabs).
       Without lipi-overlays.css the modal/drawer markup renders without
       position:fixed, no centering, no backdrop, no box-shadow — appears as
       loose elements stacked at the bottom of the page. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/lipi-overlays.css?v=20260526" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/lipi-dynamic-tabs.css?v=20260526" />

    @* Phase 2.7 — Feedback Components family (A35):
       - lipi-skeleton.css: shared shimmer keyframe + 3 shape classes for
         LipiSkeletonLine / LipiSkeletonCircle / LipiSkeletonRect. Without this
         file, the three primitives render as invisible empty spans.
       - lipi-validation.css: global @keyframes lipi-field-flash + .lipi-field-flash
         class. This must be global (not scoped) because the flash effect
         targets ANY input element on the page, not just elements rendered by
         LipiValidationSummary itself. Loaded after component CSS so it can
         override input ring shadows during the 1.5s flash animation. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/lipi-skeleton.css?v=20260526" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/lipi-validation.css?v=20260526" />

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="LiPi.Web.styles.css" />

    <style>
        .loading-spinner {
            position: fixed;
            top: 50%;
            left: 50%;
            transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
            width: 50px;
            height: 50px;
            border: 4px solid rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.2);
            border-top-color: #06b6d4;
            border-radius: 50%;
            animation: spin 0.8s linear infinite;
        }
        @@keyframes spin {
            to { transform: translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(360deg); }
        }
    </style>

    @*
        FOUC PREVENTION — MUST be blocking script (no async/defer), MUST be in <head>.
        Runs before browser paints content.
    *@
    <script src="js/theme-switcher.js?v=20260526"></script>

    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="@InteractiveServer" />
</head>
<body>
    @* CRITICAL: <CascadingAuthenticationState> wrapper required for SSR
       prerender + interactive circuit auth flow. Do not remove — removal
       breaks authentication on initial page load. See
       docs/00-PROJECT-BASELINE.md §Development & Debugging. *@
    <CascadingAuthenticationState>
        <ThemeProvider>
            <Router AppAssembly="@typeof(App).Assembly">
                <Found Context="routeData">
                    <AuthorizeRouteView RouteData="@routeData" DefaultLayout="@typeof(LiPi.Web.Components.MainLayout)">
                        <NotAuthorized>
                            <LiPi.Web.Components.RedirectToLogin />
                        </NotAuthorized>
                    </AuthorizeRouteView>
                    <FocusOnNavigate RouteData="@routeData" Selector="h1" />
                </Found>
                <NotFound>
                    <PageTitle>Not Found</PageTitle>
                    <LayoutView Layout="@typeof(LiPi.Web.Components.MainLayout)">
                        <div class="container text-center mt-5">
                            <h1>Page Not Found</h1>
                            <p>The page you're looking for doesn't exist.</p>
                            <a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Go Home</a>
                        </div>
                    </LayoutView>
                </NotFound>
            </Router>
        </ThemeProvider>
    </CascadingAuthenticationState>

    @* Body scripts — order preserved; theme-switcher.js is in <head>, not here.
       Cache version added to ALL JS scripts in this batch — previously only CSS was versioned. *@
    <script src="js/lipi-login.js?v=20260526"></script>
    <script src="js/lipi-topnav.js?v=20260526"></script>
    <script src="js/lipi-shortcuts.js?v=20260526"></script>

    @* Phase 2.2: input family helpers (autogrow Batch 3, selectAll Batch 4).
       Loaded BEFORE blazor.web.js so window.lipiInput is available when components first render. *@
    <script src="js/lipi-input.js?v=20260526"></script>

    @* Phase 2.6.2: overlay surfaces JS interop (focus trap stack, ghost-click guard,
       body scroll lock with scrollbar compensation, page-inert helper, bfcache pageshow
       reload, document-level Escape listener registration).
       Loaded BEFORE blazor.web.js so window.lipiOverlay is available when overlay
       components (LipiOverlayHost, LipiDrawer) first render. Without this script,
       FocusTrapService / ScrollLockService / setPageInert calls throw JSException
       which is silently swallowed — overlays render but keyboard/scroll behaviors
       degrade silently. *@
    <script src="js/lipi-overlay-interop.js?v=20260526"></script>

    @* Phase 2.7 (A35): validation summary click-to-field interop. Exposes
       window.lipiValidation.scrollToField(fieldId) — used by LipiValidationSummary
       when the user clicks an error in the bulleted list. Loaded BEFORE blazor.web.js
       so window.lipiValidation is available when the summary first renders.
       Failure mode is silent: if the script doesn't load, the summary still shows
       errors, but clicking an item is a no-op. *@
    <script src="js/lipi-validation.js?v=20260526"></script>

    <script src="_framework/blazor.web.js"></script>
</body>
